course: dictionary
lesson: 4801
title: Humiliation and strong feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Humiliation is the very bad, hot feeling of shame you get when someone makes you look stupid or weak in front of others. Humiliate is the verb, and humiliating is the adjective, as in «a humiliating defeat».
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «Many in China see 1949 as the end of foreign humiliation» tells you that humiliation was a painful feeling that lasted a long time, and that the word end shows it had stopped. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try "shame" in its place and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Humiliation can be a feeling or an event. «Feel humiliation» means you feel that shame inside. «Public humiliation» means being shamed in front of other people, and in sport news a «humiliation» is a heavy defeat. The words around it show which one the writer means.
fact: Humiliation means a very bad, hot feeling of shame.
fact: «Feel humiliation» means you feel that shame inside.
fact: «Public humiliation» means being shamed in front of other people.
fact: «A humiliating defeat» is a loss so heavy that it makes you feel small.
fact: Laughing at other people's mistakes can cause humiliation, so kind people do not do it.
exercise: «Many in China see 1949 as the end of foreign humiliation.» What does humiliation mean here? | *A painful feeling of shame and weakness | A time of big celebrations and parties | A very cold winter | A new school year starting
exercise: A football team loses 10-0 in the cup final. Which phrase fits best? | A gentle breeze | A quiet library | *A humiliating defeat | A happy birthday
exercise: Which word is the verb that means to make someone feel ashamed? | *humiliate | humid | humming | human
test: Ravi's teacher laughed at his spelling in front of the whole class, and he felt terrible. What did Ravi feel? | *Humiliation | Bored and sleepy | Cold and wet | Bright and happy
test: Which phrase means being shamed in front of other people? | A sunny morning | *Public humiliation | A quiet walk | Private joy
exam: Which sentence uses humiliation correctly? | *Laughing at other people's mistakes can cause humiliation | Humiliation means running very fast | Humiliation is the colour of the sky | Humiliation is a type of sandwich
